From: timstarr@netcom.com (Tim Starr)
Date: Thu, 7 Jul 1994 21:10:51 -0700
Subject: [#94-7-51] Childhood Anecdote

Someone asked if we've got any childhod anecdotes about why/how we became
libertarians.  My mother tells me that I once asked her why we went to visit
my grandparents every summer while we were there.  She replied that she need-
ed to take some time out to figure out what she wanted in life.  I replied
that I already knew what I wanted.  Astonished, she asked me (I was less
than 5 years old at the time) what, and I said "Freedom!"

I've always been a libertarian.  For a while I thought that meant some sort
of communitarian socialism, but that probably came from growing up in
Berkeley more than anything else.  I got better.

