Subject: [#94-7-62] externalities

At  9:17 AM 7/8/94 +0800, Mr John M Casey wrote:
>I would propose that his blindness is an
>externality, a cost borne by society but not in fact borne by any
>individual in significant degree.

This is not how economists use the term externality. There are no actions
or transactions between third parties that cause Jim's blindness.

You are of course free to use the term any way you please. But if you want
to be understood, standard usage might help.

I think you're actually groping for some concept of insurance and
risk-pooling. When done voluntarily, this can be quite beneficial, though
there are the well-known problems of moral hazard and adverse selection.

Dave



